# Pipeline End Goal

Build a pipeline that can handle arbitrarily complex shots by decomposing work into the
smallest meaningful dependency-ordered units, validating each unit, and repeatedly proving
that previously accepted work still holds. Beacon Wake is a test fixture, never the design
target. The canonical rationale is in `docs/architecture/pipeline-end-goal.md`.

## Always

- Keep a layer as a department/ownership boundary; let the planner create a dynamic number
  of internal work units from the shot, references, dependencies, control families, and risk.
- Give every work unit one bounded goal, one derived write-cluster, semantic mutation scope,
  dependencies, protected contracts, evidence policy, completion clause, checkpoint, repair
  owner, and typed successor interfaces.
- Plan each work unit just in time from sealed prior outcomes instead of using one giant plan.
- Treat a wrong DAG/scope/owner as a versioned replan that preserves unaffected checkpoints,
  invalidates dependants, and marks replaced work superseded. A sibling rematerialization that
  only changes the combined layers.json hash is a preserve-all plan-identity adoption, not a
  DAG change. Consuming a typed finding reopens that unit and its affected closure without
  treating an unchanged JIT view as an empty-base add-all. Rematerialization of a layer that
  already has accepted units is that same apply_replan: matching digests stay.
- Select objects and controls by semantic roles/properties, never fragile display names.
- Validate in widening rings: mutation -> unit -> interface regression -> layer regression ->
  cross-layer regression -> full-shot acceptance. Look-less layer composition fans in those
  units' executable claims; it does not reopen a critic look vote.
- Persist scripts, manifests, measurements, verdicts, hashes, and checkpoints on disk; do not
  rely on conversation memory or critic prose as execution authority.
- Freeze a candidate before evaluation. Parallelize isolated evidence production, then fan in
  to one ordered verdict; serialize authoritative mutation, integration, accept, and rollback.
- Make every repair transactional and restore the last accepted checkpoint on regression,
  truncation, cancellation, SDK failure, or worker failure.
- Use generic evidence primitives. Derive subjects, frames, regions, targets, stages, and
  tolerances from each shot's brief and references.
- Make the active agent smarter with ground truth, instruments, context compiled to the
  work unit, and a queryable unit-scope card; do not scale by enlarging the agent session
  or asking it to rediscover authority.
- Give autonomous blocking authority only to executable or currently qualified qualitative
  claims; otherwise improve evidence/judgement or require audited human adjudication.
- Give interaction defects a bounded coordination owner; broader balancing must replan.

## Never

- Hardcode shot names, subject names, fixed frames, fixed stage counts, or Beacon-specific
  assumptions in core pipeline code.
- Treat one layer as one giant unrestricted agent session.
- Enlarge prompts or sessions as the way complexity scales, or replace evidence with a
  confident model verdict.
- Let multiple workers mutate the same scene or script concurrently.
- Let a local fix trade away an already passing frame, unit, interface, or upstream layer.
- Repair a fault in a downstream layer when its semantic owner is known upstream.
- Ship partial/unvalidated edits or call an interrupted agent result complete.
- Let rematerialization select a reverted overlay before the replacement publishes.
- Refuse rematerialization solely because a sibling unit is accepted.
- Let an exhausted session publish because a candidate file exists.
- Let a prior generation's structured decision bind the selected bundle.
- Let a materialization session invent judge frames to bind extra-frame contracts.
- Publish a keyframe schedule whose samples already exceed a same-role smoothness cap.
- Burn remaining repairs on an unsatisfiable published pair, or score look on no-signal plates.
- Rank an off-scope recipe as builder permission.
- Leave a smoothness fail as a scalar without its argmax adjacent-frame pair.
- Treat a `keyframe_schedule` path miss as INAPPLICABLE, or match sample paths only against the object action.
- Bind required `visible_fraction` on a unit that cannot change those rays (volume-only vis).
- Let a multi-role `visible_fraction` PASS while a named role is below `lo`.
- Let later geometry in the same layer seal while a sibling vis row fails.
- Default look-less live `render_frame` / `verify_change` to EEVEE.
- Persist `status.json` `detail` as the exit-code digit.
- Run a materialization session without binding a transcript.
- Reopen a critic look vote at composed canonical when every unit declared empty look capabilities.
- Treat a sibling rematerialization's combined layers.json hash as a DAG change when
  this layer's unit digests still match.
- Compare a JIT-layer falsification `plan_hash` to the sparse bundle `layers.json`.
- Leave a consumed `hypothesis_falsified` unit preserved because the published DAG
  bytes did not change.
- Teach a shared-role check_scene miss as "pass an exact role".
- Let a look-owning repair diagnose critic look from Workbench solid only.
- Leave repair `cannot_express_in_scope` only on the live blender MCP.
- Treat a 0/0 image-contract pass as critic handoff on a look unit.
- Let a unit judge frame with no required claim become a critic look vote.
- Let a look-owning unit seal 5.0 on scene counts.
- Let claim-closure retract a look `image_contract` debt as `does not exist`.
- Freeze a candidate while owed image-contract ids are unpaid without typed abstention.
- Let an f150 image measurement pay an f72 debt.
- Prefix `check:` onto unpaid-debt ids in `cannot_express` or hypothesis-falsification records.
- Compare a `check:`-prefixed falsification id to a bare contract row without stripping.
- Let a builder silently rewrite its plan, broaden repair scope, or misclassify blocked work.
- Add compatibility fallbacks that silently revive obsolete plans, schemas, selectors, or
  execution contracts; migrations are explicit and fail closed.
- Let a successor become ready from producer unit ids without declaring the consumed
  interface id and kind.
- Let authored publish-interface identity sit outside `unit_digest` so `apply_replan`
  preserves a changed producer.
- Let a dependency strip producer export roles from write-clusters or grant mutation
  of those roles.
- Collapse an unresolved write family to residual `control` when one namespace has
  mixed mutation targets.
